WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Muslims believe Allah knows and
has decreed all that happens,

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.950
good and bad.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.720
This is al-Qadr.

4
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.190
Many Sunni scholars teach that it is
all written in the Preserved Tablet.

5
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.350
Yet a man once asked whether
he should tie up his camel,

6
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.310
or simply trust in Allah.

7
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.310
If Allah already knows
every choice you make,

8
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.690
are you still free?

9
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.790
And is Judgement fair?

10
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.440
In this mission, you'll explore
how Muslims link the decree,

11
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.170
human choice and the Day of Judgement.

12
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.880
Then you'll weigh up a sharp claim:
that if Allah has decided everything,

13
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.290
it is unfair to judge people.

14
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.160
Your mission: find out how Muslims
believe people can be free,

15
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.590
and judged fairly, when
Allah knows everything.
